# text = He believed that the dissensions which he saw raging in the Church would speedily effect the destruction of Christianity itself ; that , when such a period should arrive , the public mind would require but the guidance of some superior intellect to return to its old religious predilections ; and that to lay the foundation for effecting in such a manner the desired revolution , it was necessary for him -- impossible though it might seem in his present degraded condition -- to gain access to the disaffected nobles of Rome , and discover the secret of acquiring such an influence over them as would enable him to infect them with his enthusiasm , and fire them with his determination .
