# text = Whether as he looked on Vetranio's disturbed countenance , and marked his unsteady gait , the heart of Ulpius , for the first time since his introduction to the senator , misgave him when he thought of their monstrous engagement ; or whether the near approach of the moment that was henceforth , as he wildly imagined , to fix Vetranio as his assistant and ally , so powerfully affected his mind that it instinctively sought to vent its agitation through the natural medium of words , it is useless to inquire .
