# text = He resolved as soon as night approached to begin his labours on the wall ; to seek -- if the breach were made good , and the darkness favoured him -- the tent of Alaric ; and once arrived there , to acquaint the Gothic King with the weakness of the materials for defence within the city , and dilapidated condition of the fortifications below the Pincian Mount , insisting , as the condition of his treachery , on an assurance from the barbarian leader ( which he doubted not would be gladly and instantly accorded ) of the destruction of the Christian churches , the pillage of the Christian possessions , and the massacre of the Christian priests .
