# text = Recovered from their first astonishment , they burst into a loud and universal laugh cried Fravitta , who having served in the armies of Rome , and acquired a vague knowledge there of the ancient mythology , and the modern politics of the Empire , was considered by his companions as the wit of the battalion to which he was attached growled Fritigern , a heavy , phlegmatic giant , renowned for his imperturbable good humour and his prowess in drinking interrupted Colias , a ruddy , reckless boy of sixteen , privileged to be impertinent in consideration of his years gravely demanded Athanaric , who piqued himself on his theological accomplishments and his extraordinary piety exclaimed Suerid , sarcastically cried Witheric , with an insolent laugh replied Fritigern , complacently . ' What says the chorus of the song ?
