# text = But now , when she heard the sentence of her banishment proclaimed by the very lips which but the evening before had assured her of shelter and protection , she rose up instantly , cast on the young Goth a glance of such speechless misery and despair , that he involuntarily quailed before it ; and then , without a tear or a sigh , without a look of reproach , or a word of entreaty , petrified and bowed down beneath a perfect trance of terror and grief , she left the tent .
