# text = Persuading himself that , after having delayed so long , Goisvintha would now refrain from seeking him until the morrow , and that all communications from Alaric , had they been despatched , would have reached him ere this ; unable any longer to combat his anxiety for the safety of Antonina ; determined to risk the worst possibilities rather than be absent at such a time of tempest and peril from the farm-house , he made a last visit to the stations of the watchful sentinels , and quitted the camp for the night More than an hour after Hermanric had left the encampment , a man hurriedly entered the house set apart for the young chieftain's occupation .
