# text = Opposed at all points by the force of adverse circumstances , finding his life of no further use to the culinary interests of Rome , he called his chosen friends together to assist him , conscientiously drank up every drop of wine remaining in his cellars , lit the funeral pile of himself and his guests , in the banqueting-hall of his own palace , and died , as he had lived , the patriotic CATO of his country's gastronomy cried Vetranio , pointing triumphantly to the epitaph --' behold in every line of those eloquent letters at once the seal of my resolute adherence to the engagement that unites us here , and the foundation of my just claim to the reverence of posterity on the most useful of the arts which I exercised for the benefit of my species !
