# text = So in the religion , the votary was allured by the splendour of processions ; by the pomp of auguries ; by the poetry of the superstition which peopled his native woods with the sportive Dryads , and the fountains from which he drank with their guardian Naiads ; which gave to mountain and lake , to sun and moon and stars , to all things around and above him , their fantastic allegory , or their gracious legend of beauty and love : but beyond this , his first acquaintance with his worship was not permitted to extend , here his initiation concluded .
