# text = The enthusiast for the right and the fanatic for the wrong ; the man who had toiled to reform the Church , and the man who had toiled to restore the Temple ; the master who had received and trusted the servant in his home , and the servant who in that home had betrayed the master's trust -- the two characters , separated hitherto in the sublime disunion of good and bad , now struck together in tremendous contact , as brethren who had drawn their life from one source , who as children had been sheltered under the same roof !
