# text = No remnant of his careless self-possession , his easy , patrician affability , appeared in his manner , as he now listened to his companion's conversation ; years seemed to have been added to his life since he had headed the table at ' The Banquet of Famine said the physician , a cold , calm man , who spoke much , but pronounced all his words with emphatic deliberation exclaimed Vetranio , in low , mournful tones pursued the physician sighed Vetranio bitterly to himself continued the other repeated the senator mournfully , as if he heeded not the last words said the physician , speaking in warmer tones , for he was struck with pity , in spite of himself , at the spectacle of Vetranio's utter dejection interrupted Vetranio , looking round superstitiously to the frail form on the couch The physician shook his head derisively .
