# text = The miserable contrast between what she was now and what she had been them , was beyond the passive endurance , the patient resignation of the spirit-broken old man ; the empty cup dropped from his hands , he knelt down by the side of the couch and groaned aloud cried the weak , plaintive voice above him He raised his head , and looked up at her , vacant and wistful , forlorn already , as if the death-parting was over she sighed faintly whispered the old man affrightedly said the girl tenderly repeated Numerian in the same low , vacant tones .
